{"parentUuid":"79821af1-7ff8-45b2-ad74-1f66abda6ae3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d8b963fa-dadc-413b-9392-667bd1294b0d","agentId":"acb9bd4fdd02868c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZ8DTBmjXdM4R4hRztNMNN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tail effect MIP solver \"long tail\" gap closing dual bound improvement rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"MIP: THEORY AND PRACTICE CLOSING THE GAP\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-0-387-35514-6_2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How is the optimality gap, or MIP gap, calculated? – SimpleRose Knowledge Garden\",\"url\":\"https://support.simplerose.com/hc/en-us/articles/32668122254995-How-is-the-optimality-gap-or-MIP-gap-calculated\"},{\"title\":\"class Model - Python MIP Documentation - Read the Docs\",\"url\":\"https://python-mip.readthedocs.io/en/latest/classes.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Guidelines - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/documentation/current/refman/mip_models.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to force solver in MIP problem to search for solution that is VERY close to optimal solution? I'm using MIPRELSTOP = 0, but that is not enough. I'm getting gap that is around 0.0004% and for MIPRELSTOP = 0 it is already fine.\",\"url\":\"https://community.fico.com/s/question/0D54W000096IMt9SAG/how-to-force-solver-in-mip-problem-to-search-for-solution-that-is-very-close-to-optimal-solution-im-using-miprelstop-0-but-that-is-not-enough-im-getting-gap-that-is-around-00004-and-for-miprelstop-0-it-is-already-fine\"},{\"title\":\"Quick start - Python MIP Documentation - Read the Docs\",\"url\":\"https://python-mip.readthedocs.io/en/latest/quickstart.html\"},{\"title\":\"MIP Models - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/documentation/9.0/refman/mip_models.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Reference - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/documentation/current/refman/mipgap2.html\"}]\n\nI found search results related to MIP (Mixed-Integer Programming) solver gaps and bounds, but the results focus primarily on practical implementation details about MIPGap parameters and dual bounds in solvers like Gurobi. However, the specific academic concepts you're searching for—\"tail effect,\" the \"long tail\" phenomenon in gap closing, and dual bound improvement rates—appear to require more specialized research literature.\n\nThe search results show that MIP solvers produce a sequence of improving incumbent solutions (primal bound) and estimates for the optimal cost (dual bound), and when the costs of these two bounds match the search is concluded. Additionally, increasing the heuristics parameter can lead to more and better feasible solutions, but it will also reduce the rate of progress in the best bound, which touches on tradeoffs in solver strategies.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about the \"tail effect,\" \"long tail\" gap-closing behavior, or the specific dual bound improvement rate dynamics you're asking about. These terms suggest more specialized research in MIP solver performance analysis, possibly from academic papers or technical reports from solver development teams. To find this information, you might want to search academic databases or look for recent technical papers from organizations like the COIN-OR project or commercial solver vendors like Gurobi.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8ff81262-1294-4c34-849c-585254b5f660","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:45.091Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"79821af1-7ff8-45b2-ad74-1f66abda6ae3","userT